# Changelog (agents)

Vera has **no** GitHub Actions changelog bot. Agents and maintainers update `CHANGELOG.md` in the **same PR** as the change.

## When you change code or product docs

1. Edit `CHANGELOG.md` under `## Unreleased`.
2. Prefer Keep a Changelog sections: `### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Fixed`, `### Removed`, `### Documentation`.
3. Write short, user-facing bullets (what landed), not commit hashes or file lists.
4. If the PR is already numbered / known, you may also prepend under `### Merged`:
   `- [#N](https://github.com/ingmarstruijs/Vera/pull/N) — <clear title> (YYYY-MM-DD)`
5. Skip the changelog only for pure chore/meta PRs that do not affect product or process (e.g. typo in an unrelated comment). When skipping, say so in the PR body.

## When releasing

- Preview Obtainium builds (`0.1.<N>`) do **not** require folding `Unreleased`.
- For annotated `v*` tags, move relevant `## Unreleased` bullets into a new `## [X.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section (see `docs/RELEASING.md`).

## Do not

- Do **not** reintroduce `.github/workflows/changelog-on-merge.yml` or open `chore/changelog-record-*` PRs.
- Do **not** leave `CHANGELOG.md` stale while shipping user-visible or CI/release changes.
